#: docs/index.md:71
msgid "Thailand and Lao PDR never connect to each other. Both build on WHO GDHCN. Thailand publishes the key it signs certificates with, and Lao PDR caches the trust list, so its clinics can verify a Thai card with no signal. A year later the same trust list lets a Thai clinic verify the Lao VHL. Data crosses the border in only two ways: as a signed QR card the family carries, or as a link the family chooses to share. The <a0>journeys walkthrough's \"How it works\" view</a0> lays out both countries' components on the <a1>DPI-H reference architecture</a1>, with GDHCN as the foundation; the same picture as an ArchiMate overlay on the RA's own model is on the <a2>architecture page</a2>."
msgstr ""

